[0m
[32m## 2. Company & Product Overview  

[0m
[32m| Attribute | Detail |
[0m
[32m|-----------|--------|
[0m
[32m| **Company** | IGC Pharma, Inc. (NYSE American: IGC) |
[0m
[32m| **Location** | Potomac, Maryland (US) |
[0m
[32m| **Product** | **MINT‑AD** (Multimodal Interpretable Transformer for Alzheimer’s) – AI platform that integrates clinical, demographic, lifestyle, and cognitive data to predict an individual’s risk of developing AD. PRISM™ is the application layer that delivers risk scores, longitudinal health‑tracking, and clinical‑trial recruitment tools. |
[0m
[32m| **Stage** | **Marketed** (PRISM™ launched Oct 2023, pilot deployments with two health‑system partners; regulatory pathway under FDA’s Biomarker Qualification Program (BQP) – tiered, risk‑based framework). |
[0m
[32m| **Funding Goal** | **$8 M** seed round (30‑day closing target) for: <br>• Final algorithm validation (clinical‑trial data integration) <br>• Expansion of data‑science & engineering team (10 new hires) <br>• Regulatory filing support (BQP qualification) <br>• Pilot commercialization (10 000 patients) |
[0m
[32m| **Revenue Model** | SaaS licensing to health systems, pharma trial‑partner subscriptions, and consumer‑facing risk‑assessment subscription. |
[0m
[32m| **Competitive Landscape** | Competing blood‑based biomarkers (e.g., PrecivityAD®), digital‑cognitive tests, and emerging AI‑risk platforms (e.g., **NeuroAge**, **Kneu Health**). IGC’s differentiator is **multimodal AI interpretability** and integration with clinical workflows. |
[0m
[32m| **Regulatory Outlook** | FDA BQP moving toward iterative, tiered qualification (public‑data, rights‑of‑reference) reduces “all‑or‑nothing” evidentiary burden, favouring platforms like MINT‑AD ([FDA BQP White Paper, 2026](https://friendsofcancerresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/Modernizing-the-FDA-Biomarker-Qualification-Program-Strengthening-Regulatory-Clarity-and-Broadening-Biomarker-Use-in-Drug-Development-White-Paper.pdf)). |

[0m
[32m**Strategic Implications** – The product sits at the intersection of **AI‑driven health‑tech** and **biomarker‑based therapeutics**, a sector that has attracted **$6.8 B** of family‑office capital in 2025 alone (15 % of all family‑office health‑tech investments) and a **$7.4 B** surge in digital‑health funding in H1 2026, with AI‑focused deals representing > 50 % of the capital deployed ([Rock Health, 2026](https://rockhealth.com/insights/h1-2026-funding-and-market-overview-durable-roots-shifting-routes/)).  

