[0m
[32m## 3. Market & Regulatory Context  

[0m
[32m### 3.1 Addressable Population  

[0m
[32m- **817 425** biomarker‑eligible early‑AD patients across the USA, EU27, UK, and Japan (≈ 0.2 % of the total population) provide a clear denominator for risk‑assessment market sizing ([Biostock Analytics, 2026](https://biostock.se/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/alzinova-ab-commissioned-valuation-analysis-biostock-analytics.pdf)).  

[0m
[32m- Assuming a **10 % market penetration** within five years (≈ 81 700 patients) and a **$150 /yr SaaS** subscription, the addressable revenue stream exceeds **$12 M** annually, with upside from pharma trial‑partner contracts (potential $5‑10 M per year).  

[0m
[32m### 3.2 FDA Biomarker Qualification Program (BQP)  

[0m
[32m- The FDA’s new tiered, risk‑based qualification framework allows **iterative validation** using publicly available data and consortium‑generated evidence, reducing the “all‑or‑nothing” evidentiary burden for AI biomarkers ([FDA BQP White Paper, 2026](https://friendsofcancerresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/Modernizing-the-FDA-Biomarker-Qualification-Program-Strengthening-Regulatory-Clarity-and-Broadening-Biomarker-Use-in-Drug-Development-White-Paper.pdf)).  

[0m
[32m- This environment favours **early‑stage AI platforms** that can demonstrate incremental performance improvements, making seed investors more comfortable with regulatory risk.  

[0m
[32m### 3.3 Funding Trends in AI‑Enabled Health‑Tech  

[0m
[32m| Year | Total US Digital‑Health Funding | % AI‑focused | Median Deal Size |
[0m
[32m|------|--------------------------------|--------------|------------------|
[0m
[32m| 2025 H1 | $6.4 B (245 deals) | 37 % | $12 M |
[0m
[32m| 2026 H1 | $7.4 B (244 deals) | 54 % | $14 M |
[0m
[32m| 2026 Q1 | $5.34 B (105 deals) – 18 mega‑deals ≥$100 M (45 % of capital) | — | $56 M (average) |

[0m
[32mThe **concentration of capital** in a handful of mega‑deals underscores the importance of **strategic, domain‑expert investors** who can provide not only capital but also **clinical partnership pathways** (e.g., pharma, health‑system pilots).  

[0m
[32m### 3.4 Maryland‑Specific Incentives  

[0m
[32m- **Maryland Biotechnology Investment Tax Credit (BIITC)** offers a **33 % credit** on qualified investments up to $250 k per investment (later amendments reference 50 % for certain cases) for “qualified Maryland biotechnology companies” (≤ 50 employees, ≤ 12 years in business, Maryland HQ) ([BIITC Statute, 2022](https://commerce.maryland.gov/Documents/FinanceDocument/BIITC-Statute.pdf)).  

[0m
[32m- **TEDCO Seed Fund** requires a Maryland principal place of business and at least one full‑time employee, making IGC Pharma eligible ([TEDCO Eligibility, 2023](https://dlslibrary.state.md.us/publications/TEDCO/EC10-415%28b%29_2023%281%29.pdf)).  

[0m
[32mThese incentives can **enhance investor returns** and lower effective cost of capital for Maryland‑based seed rounds.  

